      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
